+# Bug Fix: Preserve orders after customer deletion and fix admin pagination
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Order reads no longer require the customer entity to exist. Customer-order lookup uses the persisted customer ID, while order details continue to expose persisted billing, delivery, and email data with a null customer after deletion. Admin pagination now applies customer filtering, correct zero-based offsets, correct page counts, and stable totals for empty pages.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` | modified | Lists orders by scalar customer ID and only adds a customer object when the account still exists. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Treats missing order customers as optional and preserves list metadata/empty arrays. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java` | modified | Adds customer ID filtering, groups OR filters correctly, and retains metadata for zero matches. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java` | modified | Calculates page totals with ceiling arithmetic. |
+| `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/common/EntityList.java` | modified | Returns the actual zero page count for an empty result. |
+| `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/business/utils/RepositoryHelperTest.java` | added | Covers zero-based pagination, ceiling page counts, and empty totals. |
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- `RepositoryHelperTest.paginatesZeroBasedPagesAndCalculatesCeilingPageCount` — pins down page 1 offset and 26/25 = 2 pages.
+- `RepositoryHelperTest.keepsZeroTotalsForAnEmptyResultSet` — pins down zero pages and zero records for no matches.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=RepositoryHelperTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed; 2 tests, 0 failures.
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-shop -am -DskipTests package` → passed; all six reactor modules compiled and packaged.
+- Manual checks: reviewed the order detail populator and order model to confirm billing, delivery, and email remain sourced from the order; no end-to-end server/database fixture was available.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+- Expanded the listed pagination changes to `sm-core-model/.../EntityList.java` after the existing getter was found to convert a true zero-page count into one page, which violated the requested contract.
+- Added the missing `customerId` predicate to the modern order repository query and retained legacy start/count pagination for customer-specific lookup so the endpoint can query deleted IDs without changing its existing request shape.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Run the private order API flow against a configured database with a deleted customer and multiple orders to validate serialization and authorization end-to-end.
